        <item><title>Glassy Host 0.2.2</title><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 23:14:07 +0000</pubDate><link>https://github.com/Bunn/GlassyDesk-Host/releases/tag/v0.2.2</link><sparkle:version>6</sparkle:version><sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.2</sparkle:shortVersionString><sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion><description>&lt;p&gt;Maintenance rebuild of Glassy Host for macOS 14 and later. Streaming, pairing, and update behavior are unchanged from version 0.2.1.&lt;/p&gt;</description><enclosure url="https://github.com/Bunn/GlassyDesk-Host/releases/download/v0.2.2/GlassyHost-0.2.2.zip" length="4584085" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="aOyZRnDOoB5VS8GNllaByLjn+czMLuHKI4I7vpkZFBa2c4CSosmOXueb1Jbqk3JVqELSrzHXd3d1oxlYqIw1Dg==" /></item><item><title>Glassy Host 0.2.1</title><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 23:27:08 +0000</pubDate><link>https://github.com/Bunn/GlassyDesk-Host/releases/tag/v0.2.1</link><sparkle:version>5</sparkle:version><sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.1</sparkle:shortVersionString><sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion><description>&lt;p&gt;Glassy Host now offers a compatibility QR code for older Glassy Desk clients, using the preferred active Tailscale or VPN route. Current clients continue to use secure identity-bound pairing with automatic LAN, Tailscale, and WireGuard route selection.&lt;/p&gt;</description><enclosure url="https://github.com/Bunn/GlassyDesk-Host/releases/download/v0.2.1/GlassyHost-0.2.1.zip" length="4584078" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="hyGjp60X+7rEEGdGIspKFp++TYjVZXGpBiZK44D9cF9pRyXUjB9JRFgJ2M2xKnYCG1JDGeWQeNBMzz00/Cp8Dw==" /></item><item>
            <title>0.2.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:33:51 +0100</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Bunn/GlassyDesk-Host/releases/tag/v0.2.0</link>
            <description>&lt;p&gt;A redesigned native Mac interface, simpler QR pairing, and individual device access controls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;QR scanning requires the updated Glassy Desk client. Existing code/password pairing and saved-device authentication remain compatible.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
